==Italian==

===Toponym===
{{it-noun|f}}, toponym of [[Langobard]] or [[Late_Latin|Late Latin]] origin. 
#It defined a wooded area designated for woodcutting. These are precisely defined in the first tome of Antiquitates Italicae Medii Aevi, year '''1005''', column 183 written by Ludovico Antonio Muratori in 1738-43. It was then further defined as '''Silva cædua (Latin)''' in the Du Cange, et al., Glossarium mediae et infimae Latinitatis, Niort: L. Favre, 1883–1887 (10 vol.). These wooded areas were often deforested to make room for urban settlements and cultivated countryside.

